prompt:
You are a formal verification assistant. The following Dafny program fails Dafny verification.

=== PROGRAM ===
function isMax(m: int, numbers: seq<int>): bool
{
    m in numbers &&
    forall i :: 0 <= i < |numbers| ==> numbers[i] <= m

}

method max(numbers: seq<int>) returns (result: int)
requires numbers != []
ensures isMax(result, numbers)
{
    result := numbers[0];
    for i := 1 to |numbers|
    invariant isMax(result, numbers[0..i])
    {
        if numbers[i] > result {
            result := numbers[i];
        }
    }
}

method rolling_max(numbers: seq<int>) returns (result: seq<int>)
requires numbers != []
ensures |result| == |numbers|
ensures forall i :: 0 < i < |result| ==> isMax(result[i], numbers[0..(i+1)])
{
    var m := numbers[0];
    result := [m];
    for i := 1 to |numbers|
    invariant |result| == i
    invariant m == result[i-1]
    {
        if numbers[i] > m {
            m := numbers[i];
        }
        result := result + [m];
    }
}

=== DAFNY ERROR ===
program.dfy(26,0): Error: a postcondition could not be proved on this return path

program.dfy(25,8): Related location: this is the postcondition that could not be proved
   |
25 | ensures forall i :: 0 < i < |result| ==> isMax(result[i], numbers[0..(i+1)])
   |         ^^^^^^

Dafny program verifier finished with 3 verified, 1 error

=== COUNTEREXAMPLE ===
At initial state: numbers[0] = 9, |numbers| = 611. At a program state: m = 9. At a program state: m = 9, numbers[0] = 9, |numbers| = 611.

Analyze the failure and respond with ONLY a valid JSON object — no explanation, no markdown, no code fences. Use exactly this structure:

{
  "spec_element": "<one of: requires | invariant | ensures>",
  "proof_obligation": "<one of: initiation | preservation | bridge>",
  "diagnosis": "<explanation of what broke and why>",
  "repair": "<the corrected Dafny specification line that restores the intended behavior>"
}

Definitions:
- requires: the precondition that must hold before the method executes
- invariant: the loop invariant that must hold throughout the loop
- ensures: the postcondition that the method must guarantee on return
- initiation: the precondition does not establish the invariant at loop entry
- preservation: the loop body does not maintain the invariant
- bridge: the invariant and loop exit condition do not imply the postcondition

raw_response:
{
  "spec_element": "invariant",
  "proof_obligation": "bridge",
  "diagnosis": "The loop invariant only tracks |result| == i and m == result[i-1], but never records that earlier elements of result are maxima of the corresponding prefixes of numbers. At loop exit (i == |numbers|), the verifier knows the last element equals m but has no fact about result[1] through result[|numbers|-1] being maxima, so it cannot discharge the postcondition forall i :: 0 < i < |result| ==> isMax(result[i], numbers[0..(i+1)]).",
  "repair": "invariant forall j :: 1 <= j < i ==> isMax(result[j], numbers[0..(j+1)])"
}
